meta {
  name: Space Import Repo
  type: http
  seq: 176
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.space.importRepo
  body: binary
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/vnd.dasl.star
}

body:binary {
  @file: {{spaceRepoStarFilePath}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  spaceRepoStarFilePath: ./space-repo.star
}

docs {
  Import the authenticated account's space repo from the STAR archive com.atproto.space.getRepo
  exported on the old host. The archive names its own space and repo. The account must be
  deactivated, as for com.atproto.repo.importRepo, and the token needs a grant over the whole
  space (read, plus create/update/delete on every collection).

  The repo becomes exactly the archive's records, under a fresh rev with an empty oplog, and no
  write notification fires. Blobs are not carried: list them on the source with
  space.listBlobs and upload them. If the account is the space's authority, import the space
  first with space.importSpaceMeta.

  Errors: 400 InvalidRepoFile (malformed, or the records do not match the commit), 400
  RepoMismatch (another account's repo), 400 SpaceNotFound (the authority's space is not
  imported yet), 403 when the account is active.
}
